course: dictionary
lesson: 15189
title: Words about the body and nature
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A secretion is a liquid that a living thing makes and lets out. Your body makes secretions, and so do plants and animals. The word comes from secrete, which means to make and release, so a secretion is the thing that gets released.
explain: «The secretion of saliva starts the work of digesting your food.» Here the secretion is the saliva itself. The word tells you the body makes it, not the mouth or the food.
explain: «Sweat is a secretion that helps to cool you down on a hot day.» When you meet secretion in a text, ask: is this a liquid that a living thing makes and lets out? If yes, you have found a secretion.
fact: A secretion is a liquid made by a living thing and released from its body.
fact: Secretion can also mean the process of making and releasing such a liquid.
fact: Saliva, sweat, tears, mucus and sap are all secretions.
fact: «Snail slime» is a secretion that helps a snail move smoothly over the ground.
fact: Spiders secrete silk, and «sticky secretions» help a web catch flies.
exercise: «The snail left a shiny trail as it crawled.» The trail is a secretion. What is a secretion? | A hard stone | *A liquid that a living thing makes and lets out | A kind of cloud | A leaf that has fallen from a tree
exercise: Which of these is a secretion made by the body? | Hair | Bone | Fingernail | *Saliva
exercise: Copy the word from this sentence that names a secretion: «Sap flows slowly through the tree.» | Flows | *Sap | Through | Tree
test: Lena says a secretion is a hard rock found in caves. Is she right? | No, it is a loud noise | Yes, it is a type of plant | *No, a secretion is a liquid made by a living thing | Yes, it is a kind of stone
test: «The secretion of tears keeps your eyes clean and wet.» What do tears do for your eyes? | *They keep your eyes clean and moist | They make your eyes shut tight | They change the colour of your eyes | They make your eyes bigger
exam: Which example shows the process of secretion, not just the liquid? | A puddle of rain on the path | A bowl of hot soup | *A gland making sweat to cool the body | A dry leaf on the ground
